      "recommended_risk": "low",
      "technical_explanation": "The scanner correlated network retrieval (fetch) with a code execution sink in the same file. Examining the actual code, all fetch calls target either same-origin local avatar paths (/characters/..., user avatar URL) or SillyTavern's own backend endpoint /api/backends/chat-completions/generate. No external URLs are contacted. The only timing-related primitive is setTimeout with an inline arrow-function callback, which is not a dynamic code execution sink (no eval, no new Function, no string-based setTimeout). The request body includes reverse_proxy and proxy_password sourced from oai_settings, which is standard SillyTavern extension practice for proxying model requests through the backend. Data flow is confined to local SillyTavern APIs and the user-configured model provider via the backend. No concealed execution, exfiltration, or untrusted-input-driven code execution is present.",
